      "title": "Airbnb Is Building a \u2018Company Brain\u2019 for AI Agents with Ahmad Al-Dahle - #781",
      "summary": "AI agents need the institutional knowledge experienced employees rely on: why a system works a certain way, which policies apply, and what never made it into the documentation. Capturing that knowledge is hard. Keeping it useful as people and agents add more may be harder. In this episode, Ahmad Al-Dahle, CTO of Airbnb, shares how his team is building Project Everest, a \u201ccompany brain\u201d that captures knowledge from employees\u2019 workflows for AI agents. We explore stale information and context poisoning, why too much context can backfire, and how the team evaluates whether shared knowledge improves engineering work. We also discuss measuring AI productivity beyond token usage and PR counts, the limits of chat-based interfaces, and deploying support agents in a marketplace where resolving disputes means mediating between conflicting interests. \ud83d\uddd2\ufe0f Full show notes: https://twimlai.com/go/781 .",
      "summary_html": "<p>AI agents need the institutional knowledge experienced employees rely on: why a system works a certain way, which policies apply, and what never made it into the documentation. Capturing that knowledge is hard. Keeping it useful as people and agents add more may be harder.\n\nIn this episode, Ahmad Al-Dahle, CTO of Airbnb, shares how his team is building Project Everest, a \u201ccompany brain\u201d that captures knowledge from employees\u2019 workflows for AI agents. We explore stale information and context poisoning, why too much context can backfire, and how the team evaluates whether shared knowledge improves engineering work.\n\nWe also discuss measuring AI productivity beyond token usage and PR counts, the limits of chat-based interfaces, and deploying support agents in a marketplace where resolving disputes means mediating between conflicting interests.\n\n\ud83d\uddd2\ufe0f\u00a0Full show notes: <a href=\"https://twimlai.com/go/781\">https://twimlai.com/go/781.</a></p>",
